slowed 69%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133924103.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Sea otters returned to California’s Elkhorn Slough in 1984 when pollution had severely affected its ecosystem. Their recovery triggered changes across the food web, helping eelgrass beds expand by 600%. A later study found marsh-edge erosion slowed by an average of 69%, as otters reduced populations of root-eating crabs.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/sea-otters-returned-to-a-polluted-california-estuary-in-1984-eelgrass-expanded-600-while-marsh-edge-erosion-later-slowed-by-69-on-average/articleshow/133924103.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/sea-otters-returned-to-a-polluted-california-estuary-in-1984-eelgrass-expanded-600-while-marsh-edge-erosion-later-slowed-by-69-on-average/articleshow/133924103.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133925137,imgsize-73524.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[144-year-old Indiana train depot being restored after decades of abandonment]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133931023.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-train-depot-built-144-years-ago-sat-abandoned-for-decades-after-a-nonprofit-bought-it-in-2023-the-station-is-being-restored-as-the-centerpiece-of-a-new-railroad-campus/articleshow/133931023.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-train-depot-built-144-years-ago-sat-abandoned-for-decades-after-a-nonprofit-bought-it-in-2023-the-stat