e><![CDATA[Jeremy Corbyn finds buyer for £700,000 North London home after 19 years, nearly doubling 2007 price]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133976758.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jeremy Corbyn has found a buyer for his three-bedroom Finsbury Park home after 19 years. The former Labour leader bought the North London property for £363,000 in 2007 and initially listed it for £800,000 this year. The house was later reduced to offers over £700,000 and is now under offer, according to reports.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/jeremy-corbyn-finds-a-buyer-for-north-london-home-at-700000-after-19-years-former-labour-leader-bought-finsbury-park-house-for-363000-in-2007-after-initially-listing-it-for-800000/articleshow/133976758.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/jeremy-corbyn-finds-a-buyer-for-north-london-home-at-700000-after-19-years-former-labour-leader-bought-finsbury-park-house-for-363000-in-2007-after-initially-listing-it-for-800000/articleshow/133976758.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T22:20:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133977057,imgsize-155755.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Claire Jiang, 18-year-old NJ student diagnosed with arthritis who built a lab model of the disease]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133935974.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable achievement, eighteen-year-old student Claire Jiang claimed seventh place and a generous seventy thousand dollars for her outstanding research. Motivated by her own struggle with juvenile idiopathic arthritis, Jiang developed an innovative laboratory cell model that promises to enhance the testing of new treatments. Her success underscores the vital role of personal experiences in fostering impactful scientific advancements.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-claire-jiang-the-18-year-old-new-jersey-student-diagnosed-with-juvenile-arthritis-in-third-grade-who-built-a-lab-model-of-the-disease-her-research-won-70000/articleshow/133935974.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-claire-jiang-the-18-year-old-new-jersey-student-diagnosed-with-juvenile-arthritis-in-third-grade-who-built-a-lab-model-of-the-disease-her-research-won-70000/articleshow/133935974.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T22:00:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133937201,imgsize-632698.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Built in 1917, historic 22-bedroom hotel is up for sale]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133974764.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A historic 22-bedroom Palace Hotel in Odessa, Washington, is now for sale.  This landmark building, built in 1917, awaits a new owner.  The property spans 4,572 square feet and retains original craftsmanship.  After years of vacancy, the hotel needs significant updating and restoration.  It offers potential for various redevelopment projects and ventures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/built-in-1917-a-22-bedroom-washington-hotel-was-run-by-one-family-for-50-years-now-this-century-old-building-is-listed-for-just-195000/articleshow/133974764.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/built-in-1917-a-22-bedroom-washington-hotel-was-run-by-one-family-for-50-years-now-this-century-old-building-is-listed-for-just-195000/articleshow/133974764.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T21:10:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133974915,imgsize-338470.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Highway 141 takes Missouri family’s 15 acres; how $238,000 offer became $2.1 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133968882.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Missouri family's 15-acre property, bought in 1904, became the centre of a long eminent domain dispute after St. Louis County acquired it for a highway project. A jury valued the land at $1.3 million, while the court added $650,000 in heritage value and interest, taking the judgment to about $2.1 million. The Missouri Supreme Court later upheld the award.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1904-a-missouri-family-acquired-15-acres-106-years-later-st-louis-county-condemned-it-for-highway-141-and-a-238000-offer-became-a-2-1-million-judgment-upheld-on-appeal/articleshow/133968882.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1904-a-missouri-family-acquired-15-acres-106-years-later-st-louis-county-condemned-it-for-highway-141-and-a-238000-offer-became-a-2-1-million-judgment-upheld-on-appeal/articleshow/133968882.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T20:57:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133970516,imgsize-148972.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Couple bought a broken Eichler home; now it’s worth $2.75 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133973166.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A magnificent example of midcentury modern architecture, this rare 1971 Eichler home in San Anselmo is listed at $2.75 million. Boasting four bedrooms, it has been tastefully renovated since its acquisition in 2015, showcasing an inviting indoor-outdoor aesthetic, a contemporary kitchen, and a sparkling pool. This home blends vibrant living spaces, making it perfect for families and older adults seeking style and comfort.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2015-a-california-couple-bought-a-distressed-1971-eichler-home-at-auction-11-years-later-their-fully-restored-house-one-of-just-15-eichlers-in-the-area-is-asking-2-75m/articleshow/133973166.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2015-a-california-couple-bought-a-distressed-1971-eichler-home-at-auction-11-years-later-their-fully-restored-house-one-of-just-15-eichlers-in-the-area-is-asking-2-75m/articleshow/133973166.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T20:12:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133973232,imgsize-426080.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump gives Natalie Harp, 2 aides $45,000 each: Why cash gifts are under scrutiny]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133973454.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-gives-natalie-harp-2-aides-45000-each-why-cash-gifts-for-holidays-are-under-scrutiny/articleshow/133973454.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-gives-natalie-harp-2-aides-45000-each-why-cash-gifts-for-holidays-are-under-scrutiny/articleshow/133973454.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T20:27:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133973655,imgsize-72437.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New satellite images show major construction surge at Iran’s Pickaxe nuke site]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133967582.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Construction activity has significantly increased at Iran's underground Pickaxe Mountain nuclear site this year.  The United States is developing new weapons to target deeply buried facilities.  President Trump has repeatedly threatened strikes on the heavily fortified Iranian location.  The US military maintains operational plans for potential strikes against the site.  This renewed scrutiny occurs as the wider US-Iran conflict intensifies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/satellite-images-show-major-construction-surge-at-irans-underground-pickaxe-site-amid-us-war/articleshow/133967582.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/satellite-images-show-major-construction-surge-at-irans-underground-pickaxe-site-amid-us-war/articleshow/133967582.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T17:42:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133968603,imgsize-1002898.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[IT giants' PERM filings suspended: What does this mean for Green Card applicants?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133972511.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/it-giants-perm-filings-suspended-what-does-this-mean-for-green-card-applicants/articleshow/133972511.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/it-giants-perm-filings-suspended-what-does-this-mean-for-green-card-applicants/articleshow/133972511.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T19:44:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133972545,imgsize-42784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado man challenges drilling rights beneath his mountain as 400,000 acres head to lease sales]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133967241.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Colorado landowner and Desert Storm veteran is continuing his legal fight against oil and gas drilling rights beneath Baker’s Peak after the Bureau of Land Management rejected his protest. His appeal comes as the BLM prepares to offer more than 400,000 acres of Colorado land for drilling across six lease sales through December 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-motorcycle-instructor-and-desert-storm-veteran-challenged-drilling-rights-beneath-his-mountain-after-regulators-rejected-him-he-kept-fighting-as-more-than-400000-acres-head-toward-oil-and-gas-lease-sales/articleshow/133967241.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-motorcycle-instructor-and-desert-storm-veteran-challenged-drilling-rights-beneath-his-mountain-after-regulators-rejected-him-he-kept-fighting-as-more-than-400000-acres-head-toward-oil-and-gas-lease-sales/articleshow/133967241.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133968735,imgsize-114144.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[10,000 homes were demolished to build world’s heaviest building in Romania; the story behind it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133970692.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bucharest’s grand Palace of the Parliament, commissioned by dictator Nicolae Ceaușescu, looms large as a testament to an ambitious and controversial regime. The construction, initiated in 1984, involved the demolition of historic districts, displacing tens of thousands of citizens. Notably, it is the heaviest administrative building worldwide, although much of it remains unoccupied. The colossal structure's fate is precarious as it continues to sink slightly each year.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1984-romanian-dictator-ordered-the-construction-of-a-giant-palace-in-bucharest-demolishing-10000-homes-today-the-palace-of-the-parliament-stands-as-the-worlds-heaviest-building-that-is-slowly-sinking-every-year/articleshow/133970692.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1984-romanian-dictator-ordered-the-construction-of-a-giant-palace-in-bucharest-demolishing-10000-homes-today-the-palace-of-the-parliament-stands-as-the-worlds-heaviest-building-that-is-slowly-sinking-every-year/articleshow/133970692.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T18:56:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133971033,imgsize-1467150.cms"/></item></channel></rss>